WEBVTT

00:00:00.367 --> 00:00:02.900
Are you a SMART fella,

00:00:02.900 --> 00:00:04.933
or a FART smella?

00:00:04.933 --> 00:00:06.433
Let's find OUT!

00:00:07.600 --> 00:00:09.400
Check this out,

00:00:09.400 --> 00:00:11.200
a word analogy!

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:13.600
Hot is to cold,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:16.000
as day is to...

00:00:16.000 --> 00:00:16.600
what?

00:00:16.600 --> 00:00:17.200
A.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:17.800
Morning,

00:00:17.800 --> 00:00:18.400
B.

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:19.000
Night,

00:00:19.000 --> 00:00:19.600
C.

00:00:19.600 --> 00:00:20.200
Sun,

00:00:20.200 --> 00:00:21.400
or D.

00:00:21.400 --> 00:00:22.000
Light?

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.200
Five seconds!

00:00:29.000 --> 00:00:30.200
TIME'S UP!

00:00:30.867 --> 00:00:31.300
It's...

00:00:31.300 --> 00:00:31.767
B,

00:00:31.767 --> 00:00:32.200
night!

00:00:32.200 --> 00:00:34.400
Hot and cold are opposites,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:37.067
so the opposite of day is

00:00:37.067 --> 00:00:37.500
night.

00:00:37.500 --> 00:00:40.133
It is the same relationship, flipped.

00:00:41.300 --> 00:00:41.933
Okay,

00:00:41.933 --> 00:00:43.833
a number series!

00:00:43.833 --> 00:00:44.467
Two,

00:00:44.467 --> 00:00:45.067
three,

00:00:45.067 --> 00:00:45.700
five,

00:00:45.700 --> 00:00:46.333
eight,

00:00:46.333 --> 00:00:46.967
thirteen,

00:00:46.967 --> 00:00:48.233
and then...

00:00:48.233 --> 00:00:50.133
what comes next?

00:00:50.133 --> 00:00:50.767
A.

00:00:50.767 --> 00:00:51.400
Eighteen,

00:00:51.400 --> 00:00:52.033
B.

00:00:52.033 --> 00:00:52.633
Twenty,

00:00:52.633 --> 00:00:53.267
C.

00:00:53.267 --> 00:00:53.900
Twenty-one,

00:00:53.900 --> 00:00:55.167
or D.

00:00:55.167 --> 00:00:55.800
Twenty-six?

00:00:55.800 --> 00:00:57.067
Five seconds!

00:01:02.833 --> 00:01:04.033
TIME'S UP!

00:01:04.700 --> 00:01:06.233
The answer is...

00:01:06.233 --> 00:01:06.733
C,

00:01:06.733 --> 00:01:07.267
twenty-one!

00:01:07.267 --> 00:01:10.300
Add the two numbers before it:

00:01:10.300 --> 00:01:12.867
eight plus thirteen is twenty-one.

00:01:12.867 --> 00:01:15.433
It is the add-the-last-two pattern.

00:01:16.567 --> 00:01:17.700
Here's one,

00:01:17.700 --> 00:01:19.400
a shape puzzle!

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:21.633
Which shape comes next?

00:01:21.633 --> 00:01:22.200
A.

00:01:22.200 --> 00:01:23.333
A triangle,

00:01:23.333 --> 00:01:23.900
B.

00:01:23.900 --> 00:01:25.000
A square,

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:25.567
C.

00:01:25.567 --> 00:01:26.700
A circle,

00:01:26.700 --> 00:01:27.833
or D.

00:01:27.833 --> 00:01:28.967
A pentagon?

00:01:28.967 --> 00:01:30.100
Five seconds!

00:01:35.867 --> 00:01:37.067
TIME'S UP!

00:01:37.733 --> 00:01:39.167
The answer is...

00:01:39.167 --> 00:01:39.667
A,

00:01:39.667 --> 00:01:40.600
a triangle!

00:01:40.600 --> 00:01:43.500
The sides count down by one:

00:01:43.500 --> 00:01:44.467
hexagon six,

00:01:44.467 --> 00:01:45.400
pentagon five,

00:01:45.400 --> 00:01:46.367
square four,

00:01:46.367 --> 00:01:49.267
so next is the triangle with

00:01:49.267 --> 00:01:50.200
three sides.

00:01:51.367 --> 00:01:51.767
So,

00:01:51.767 --> 00:01:53.800
are you smart or fart?

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:56.233
Count up your correct answers to

00:01:56.233 --> 00:01:57.433
find your rank!

00:01:58.600 --> 00:01:58.933
So,

00:01:58.933 --> 00:02:00.333
how did you do?

00:02:00.333 --> 00:02:01.700
Comment your score below,

00:02:01.700 --> 00:02:03.067
and follow for more!
